    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d149">

                <pb facs="0379" n="348" sameAs="frus:frus1977-80v26/pg348"/>

                <head>149. Memorandum From Secretary of Defense Brown to the President’s Assistant
                    for National Security Affairs (Brzezinski)<anchor n="1" xml:id="d149-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1977-03-05">March 5, 1977</date>
                    </dateline></opener>
                <list subtype="subject" type="description">
                    <label>SUBJECT</label>
                    <item>Conversation with The President on CTB Considerations</item>
                </list>
                <p>At your suggestion, I conveyed my misgivings about the peaceful nuclear
                    explosions loophole in CTB to the President in a conversation yesterday.<anchor
                        n="2" xml:id="d149-f2"/> Moreover, I described the JCS position that a ban
                    on nuclear testing would be contrary to our national security interests. I
                    assured him that I would be working on the broadest, most balanced view possible
                    here in the Defense Department.</p>
                <p>The President agreed that CTB would be a useful topic for a luncheon discussion
                    by him with the Joint Chiefs, Charles Duncan, you and me.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#bold">Harold Brown</hi><anchor n="3" xml:id="d149-f3"/>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d149-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d149-f1-content">
                <p>Source: Carter Library, National Security Affairs, Brzezinski Material, Subject
                    File, Box 6, Comprehensive Test Ban (CTB), 3–12/77. Secret.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d149-f2" n="2" xml:id="d149-f2-content">
                <p>No record of this conversation has been found. According to the President’s Daily
                    Diary, Carter and Brown met from 4:45 to 5:20 p.m. on May 4. (Carter Library,
                    Presidential Materials)</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d149-f3" n="3" xml:id="d149-f3-content">
                <p> Brown signed “Harold” at the end of the memorandum.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
